1. ABSTRACT

The SPACE‑TIME‑REALITY Engine is a three‑layer computational system that unifies encrypted spatio‑temporal geometry, dynamical reality node evolution, and cryptographically verified event logging into a single governing differential equation. The engine ingests multi‑domain data, transforms it into curvature tensors, evolves interacting state machines, and records verified events in an immutable ledger. This white‑sheet defines the system states, governing equations, methods, simulation protocol, and visualization pipeline.

